1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:04,140
You care. But sometimes, you don’t know what to say.

2
00:00:04,750 --> 00:00:11,360
Meet Cue. An AI keyboard that uses your conversation’s context to help you reply in your own voice.

3
00:00:11,650 --> 00:00:12,800
Tap Suggest.

4
00:00:13,180 --> 00:00:15,620
No copying chats into another assistant.

5
00:00:15,900 --> 00:00:18,050
No explaining the background from scratch.

6
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:24,800
A week ago, Marcel mentioned his exams.

7
00:00:25,150 --> 00:00:28,240
Cue connects that earlier message to what he’s saying now.

8
00:00:28,700 --> 00:00:32,250
Open the source to see the message behind what Cue remembers.

9
00:00:33,300 --> 00:00:34,500
Have something in mind?

10
00:00:35,700 --> 00:00:36,550
Set a goal.

11
00:00:38,200 --> 00:00:39,300
Choose your tone.

12
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:42,720
And keep it subtle—or make it bolder.

13
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:47,400
Choose a suggestion.

14
00:00:47,600 --> 00:00:48,100
Review it.

15
00:00:48,450 --> 00:00:50,070
You decide what to send.

16
00:00:51,450 --> 00:00:55,160
Built from scratch at HackYeah by two eighteen-year-olds.

17
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:59,930
Cue. The context behind your words.
